(spoiler warning)


Well, not really.  You can get up to +5 (or 5 of an item if you are asking for
multiple quantities of an item).  But there is a random chance: the program
has a line checking for
	spe > rnd(5)
where rnd(5) is a number from 1 to 5.  If spe is too much, you don't get any
plusses at all.  Therefore, +5 has a 1/5 chance, +4 has a 2/5 chance, down
to +1 which you can always get.  +3 is merely a convenient number in the
middle which isn't _too_ unlikely.  Also, in early versions +3 was an absolute
limit which you could always get, so some people will use +3 just because
that's what they have always done.

For multiple quantities, you get it only if
	cnt < rnd(6)
(if this fails you only get one).  A simple calculation shows that your
expectation is best if you specify 3 or 4 (in either case you'll get an
average of 2).

Also, in the list of items you might want to wish for, I left out 2 things:
"uncursed ring of levitation" (it still works, although you can no longer start
out with one), and if you have 2 wishes or already have one: "uncursed ring of
polymorph" combined with "uncursed ring of polymorph control".  Some good
things to turn into are: "master lich", "vampire lord", "black dragon", "umber
hulk", "iron golem", "xorn", etc....

(Note that you may now use the #monster command to confuse monsters as an
umber hulk, and umber hulks also dig through walls,  Xorns walk through walls.
